[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_kimi-k2.6_cloud-failing-tests-trial-3[0m[0m
All 15 tests pass now. Here's what was wrong and what was fixed:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: Used exact string match (`required in user_roles`). Fixed to compare lowercase versions so role checks are case-insensitive.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: Used `and` instead of `or`, requiring the user to be both admin and owner. Fixed to `or` so either condition grants access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: Mutable default argument `initial={}` caused instances to share state. Fixed to use `None` default and copy the dict.
- `add`: Overwrote the existing quantity (`self._stock[sku] = qty`). Fixed to accumulate (`self._stock[sku] = self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`).
- `reserve`: Used `>=` so reserving exactly the available amount raised `OutOfStock`. Changed to `>` to allow reserving up to the available quantity.
- `release`: Allowed reserved count to go negative. Added a guard raising `ValueError` when releasing more than is currently reserved.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: Did not lowercase characters. Also only did a single `replace("--", "-")`, so three or more consecutive dashes weren't fully collapsed. Fixed by applying `.lower()` and looping `replace("--", "-")` until none remain.
- `truncate`: Added the suffix *after* slicing `max_len` characters, producing a string longer than `max_len`. Fixed to slice `max_len - len(suffix)` before appending the suffix.
